edPhase` pattern (`agent_agent.go:135-155`) — read those to pin the exact deliverer API (e.g. `libagent.AgentResultInfo`, deliverer method, `AgentStatusFailed` constant) before writing requirements.\n- The spec's Suggested Decomposition table proposes 4 prompts, but you decide the final count based on the spec (see your Sizing Guide). This is a small single-feature fix across two entry points plus regression tests — 2-3 prompts may be more appropriate than 4; do not split purely to match the table. Multi-prompt outputs use `1-`, `2-`, `3-` filename prefixes for execution order. Keep the spec's atomic-batch constraints in mind (the spec's own Constraints section says the fix lives in this repo's two entry points only).\n\n## Constraints from the spec you must preserve in prompts\n\n- Do not change the agent lib `github.com/bborbe/agent`\n- Fix lives in this repo's two entry points: `main.go` and `cmd/run-task/main.go`\n- `main.go` path: deliver a `Failed` result via the deliverer whose message names the phase, return without error (exit 0), keep the `AgentStatusFailed` + duration metrics recording, keep pushgateway deferred push non-fatal\n- `cmd/run-task/main.go` path: identical behavior, stays metrics-free as today\n- Regression tests in both `main_test.go` and `cmd/run-task/main_test.go` asserting delivered `Status == Failed`, message contains the phase name, and no error returned\n- `make precommit` exits 0; CHANGELOG entry under `## Unreleased`\n- Fail-loud sentinels for cross-prompt boundaries (use `Status: failed` with explicit message, never `needs_input`, for stubs depending on a prior prompt)\n- Single decision per prompt — no \"Option A or Option B\" branches in prompts\n- Pin behavior to existing primitives (existing deliverer, `AgentResultInfo`, existing test patterns in the repo) over inventing new helpers; inline load-bearing snippets (struct/interface signatures) verbatim into `<context>`\n\nReport back: the files you created (paths), the decompositio