{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-821b05caecb9035e","type":"tool_result","content":"include ../../Makefile.variables\ninclude ../../common.env\n\n# No-op so the recursive `apply` sweep from the parent Makefile.docker doesn't\n# choke on this directory. cmd/run-task is a local CLI for smoke tests, not a\n# deployable artifact.\n.PHONY: apply\napply:\n\t@echo \"skip apply for cmd/run-task (local CLI, not deployed)\"\n\n\nTASK_FILE ?= dummy-task.md\nBRANCH := dev\nCLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR ?= $(HOME)/.claude-agent\nAGENT_DIR ?= $(shell cd ../.. && pwd)/agent\nALLOWED_TOOLS ?= Grep,Read\n\n# MiniMax routing defaults. Token is fetched live from the personal teamvault\n# (secret key MOPmQL) so it never lands on disk; requires `teamvault-password`\n# from github.com/bborbe/teamvault-utils. Override any var to point elsewhere.\nANTHROPIC_BASE_URL ?= https://api.minimax.io/anthropic\nANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN ?= $(shell teamvault-password --teamvault-config $(HOME)/.teamvault.json --teamvault-key MOPmQL 2>/dev/null)\nANTHROPIC_MODEL ?= MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed\n\ngenerate-dummy-task:\n\t@echo '---' > $(TASK_FILE)\n\t@echo 'status: in_progress' >> $(TASK_FILE)\n\t@echo 'phase: planning' >> $(TASK_FILE)\n\t@echo 'title: Dummy Claude Task' >> $(TASK_FILE)\n\t@echo 'assignee: claude-agent' >> $(TASK_FILE)\n\t@echo '---' >> $(TASK_FILE)\n\t@echo '' >> $(TASK_FILE)\n\t@echo 'Report which language model is processing this task. Return a JSON object with these exact fields:' >> $(TASK_FILE)\n\t@echo '' >> $(TASK_FILE)\n\t@echo '- `model`: the model name as you know yourself (e.g. \"claude-sonnet-4-6\", \"MiniMax-M2.7\", etc.)' >> $(TASK_FILE)\n\t@echo '- `provider`: the provider/company that built you (\"Anthropic\", \"MiniMax\", etc.)' >> $(TASK_FILE)\n\t@echo '- `notes`: one sentence explaining how you identified yourself' >> $(TASK_FILE)\n\t@echo '' >> $(TASK_FILE)\n\t@echo 'Return ONLY the JSON object, no prose around it.' >> $(TASK_FILE)\n\t@echo \"generated $(TASK_FILE)\"\n\nrun-dummy-task: $(TASK_FILE)\n\t@go run -mod=mod . \\\n\t\t-task-file=$(TASK_FILE) \\\n\t\t-branch=$(BRANCH) \\\n\t\t-agent-dir=$(AGENT_DIR) \\\n\t\t-claude-config-dir=$(CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR) \\\n\t\t-anthropic-model='$(ANTHROPIC_MODEL)' \\\n\t\t-allowed-tools=$(ALLOWED_TOOLS) \\\n\t\t-anthropic-base-url='$(ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL)' \\\n\t\t-anthropic-auth-token='$(ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN)' \\\n\t\t-v=2\n===head scenario===\n# Scenario 001: Sentry Issue Happy Path (per-alert)\n\n**Purpose**: prove the agent works end-to-end on a single Sentry alert. Run before any deploy; run again after any non-trivial change.\n\n**Architecture**: the sentry-collector agent step creates one vault task per active Sentry alert; this agent is triggered per task and analyzes THAT single alert. This scenario simulates the collector by creating one task manually.\n\n**Setup**:\n- Agent `bborbe/agent-sentry-issue-analyzer` deployed to dev\n- Config CRD applied: `kubectlquant -n dev get config.agent.benjamin-borbe.de sentry-issue-analyzer` shows it\n- Sentry MCP configured with the required `mcp__sentry__*` tools in ALLOWED_TOOLS (fail-fast preflight enforces this)\n- Operator creates a synthetic Sentry-issue task manually (v0: sentry-collector not built yet)\n\n**Acceptance**: agent processes the task end-to-end (planning → execution → done) within 15 minutes; planning writes `## Analysis` (root cause + implicated `file.go:line`), execution writes `## Verdict` YAML with one of the 6 verdicts.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. **Create the task** (manual operator path — v0, simulating the watcher):\n\n   ```bash\n   vault-cli task create \"Analyze Sentry issue SENTRY-TEST-001\" \\\n     --vault Personal \\\n     --assignee sentry-issue-analyzer \\\n     --task-type sentry-issue-analyzer\n   ```\n\n   Then edit the task body to include the alert payload:\n   ```\n   sentry_link: https://seibert-group.sentry.io/issues/SENTRY-TEST-001\n   ## Stack Trace\n   panic: nil pointer dereference at pkg/foo/bar.go:42","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9ec0f1c05300d88","session_id":"8524de8b-d7ea-43c2-94e8-affce53f1549","uuid":"ba10bfd1-383e-4835-9c07-1899247c0b77","timestamp":"2026-09-03T19:32:32.698Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts from approved spec"}
