{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"aeec503807722fc25","tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9ec0f1c05300d88","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-1000/-workspace/8524de8b-d7ea-43c2-94e8-affce53f1549/tasks/aeec503807722fc25.output","summary":"Both prompt files are written and pass the self-audit. Here is the final report.\n\n## Files created\n\n- `/workspace/prompts/1-spec-001-fix-nil-result.md` — the implementation prompt (fix + regression tests)\n- `/workspace/prompts/2-spec-001-changelog-precommit.md` — the finalization prompt (CHANGELOG + `make precommit`)\n\nBoth are in the inbox (`prompts/`), not `prompts/in-progress/`.\n\n## Decomposition decisions (why 2, not the spec's 4)\n\nThe spec's Suggested Decomposition table proposes 4 prompts (fix main.go / fix run-task / tests / changelog+precommit). I collapsed this to 2:\n\n1. **Implementation + tests in one prompt** — the two entry-point changes are near-identical, coupled by the same defect, and must ship together (the spec's atomic-batch constraint says \"the fix lives in this repo's two entry points only\"). The regression tests belong with their implementation — splitting tests into their own prompt would have been a dependency-heavy no-op. The whole thing is ~20 lines of production change + two small Ginkgo specs.\n2. **CHANGELOG + `make precommit` in a separate final prompt** — the CLAUDE.md convention is to write the `## Unreleased` entry *before* the slow final gate, and the spec's AC 4/5 are distinct deliverables. Keeping the fast `make test` loop in prompt 1 separate from the slow precommit gate in prompt 2 is the natural split.\n\nPer the Sizing Guide, 2 prompts is right for a single feature (2-3 range).\n\n## Key design decisions (surfaced for the reviewer)\n\n- **Test observability was the one real ambiguity.** `main.go`'s `application.Run` builds the deliverer internally (`createDeliverer`): empty `TASK_ID` → Noop (not inspectable), non-empty → real Kafka SyncProducer (needs a broker). So an end-to-end test through `Run` cannot assert on the delivered `AgentResultInfo` without a real Kafka broker or a new injection seam. I resolved this by **extracting the nil-result delivery into an unexported `application.deliverNilResult(ctx, deliverer) error` method in both entry points** (mirroring the agent lib's `unsupportedPhase`), and unit-testing that method directly with the counterfeiter fake `github.com/bborbe/agent/mocks.AgentResultDeliverer` — the same external-mock pattern this repo already uses with `kafkamocks`. This asserts exactly what the ACs demand (`Status == Failed`, phase name in `Message`, no error) without Kafka. No new injection seam, no re-architecting.\n- **Test package changed `main_test` → `main`** in both `main_test.go` files (required to reach the unexported method). This deviates from the go-testing-guide's external-package preference; it's the standard tradeoff for testing unexported entry-point internals, and the requirements state the rationale inline.\n- **Message text kept as-is**: `\"agent run returned nil result (all steps skipped for phase %s)\"` becomes the delivered `Message` — minimal diff, still names the phase, and operators already recognize it.\n- **No `PrintResult` on the nil path** — mirrors `unsupportedPhase` (which doesn't print); the failure is diagnosable in the task body per desired behavior #3. Spec doesn't require printing.\n- **Deliver failure** returns `errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, \"deliver nil-result failure\")` — matches the spec Failure Modes table's `deliver ... failure` log signature (controller retries, bounded).\n- **No scenario prompt** — the scenario-writing four-condition test fails on condition (a): the behavior is fully unit-testable with the fake deliverer, so no `scenarios/NNN-*.md` is warranted. The operator-executable deploy checks stay on the spec's Verification ladder.\n\n## Verification of symbols (all read from real source before writing)\n\n- `agentlib.ResultDeliverer` / `DeliverResult(ctx, AgentResultInfo) error`, `AgentResultInfo{Status, Output, Message, NextPhase, ContinueToNext}`, `AgentStatusFailed = \"failed\"`, `agentlib.Result{Status, NextPhase, Message, ContinueToNext}` — from `github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.84.1`\n- `errors.Wrapf` / `errors.New` signatures — from `github.com/bborbe/errors@v1.5.21`\n- `mocks.AgentResultDeliverer` fake API (`DeliverResultReturns`, `DeliverResultCallCount`, `DeliverResultArgsForCall`) — from the lib's generated mocks\n- Sibling entry-point check: `grep` found a third `application.Run` in `cmd/create-tasks/main.go`, but it never calls `agent.Run` and has no nil-result guard — explicitly marked out-of-scope in prompt 1. `hideGit` is not set (`workflow: direct`), and no git commands appear in any `<verification>` anyway.\n\n## Docs referenced in `<context>` (in-container paths)\n\n- Prompt 1: `coding/docs/go-error-wrapping-guide.md`, `go-testing-guide.md`, `go-doc-best-practices.md`, `definition-of-done.md`; project `docs/dod.md`\n- Prompt 2: `coding/docs/changelog-guide.md`; project `docs/dod.md`\n\n## Pattern inlined because no doc exists\n\nThe \"entry point delivers a `Failed` result via the deliverer on the nil-result path\" pattern (build `Result` → `DeliverResult(AgentResultInfo{Status, Message})` → wrap deliver error → return nil) is inlined verbatim in prompt 1's `<context>`, sourced from the agent lib's own `unsupportedPhase` exemplar. There is no coding-plugin doc covering this specific entry-point pattern; since it's a direct mirror of an in-repo/live-library exemplar, inlining is appropriate — but if this recurs across agents (trade-analysis, pr-reviewer are cited as copy-paste siblings of this main.go), a short `go-agent-entry-point-result-delivery.md` guide would be worth adding later.\n\n## Constraints repeated in both prompts\n\n- Do NOT change `github.com/bborbe/agent` — fix lives in the two entry points only\n- Do not re-architect the phase model; `NextPhase: \"done\"` stays as-is\n- Pushgateway push stays non-fatal (`Warningf`, never fail the Job)\n- Do NOT commit — dark-factory handles git\n- Existing tests must still pass\n- (Prompt 1 additionally pins both Failure Modes rows: non-nil results route through `PrintResult` unchanged; deliver failures return the wrapped error, never swallowed)\n\n## Verification\n\n- Prompt 1: `make test` at repo root + per-package coverage confirming `deliverNilResult` is 100% covered (both success and error paths)\n- Prompt 2: `grep -n \"nil result\" CHANGELOG.md` above `## v0.9.1` + `make precommit` exits 0 (with the fix-then-rerun-failing-target loop per CLAUDE.md)\n\nSuggested next step: run `/audit-prompt prompts/1-spec-001-fix-nil-result.md` and `/audit-prompt prompts/2-spec-001-changelog-precommit.md` to validate before approving.","usage":{"total_tokens":0,"tool_uses":47,"duration_ms":322922},"uuid":"a95aa8f0-d9a1-4a47-ad59-0c29b3535cbc","session_id":"8524de8b-d7ea-43c2-94e8-affce53f1549"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9ec0f1c05300d88","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both prompt files are written and pass the self-audit. Here is the final report.\n\n## Files created\n\n- `/workspace/prompts/1-spec-001-fix-nil-result.md` — the implementation prompt (fix + regression tests)\n- `/workspace/prompts/2-spec-001-changelog-precommit.md` — the finalization prompt (CHANGELOG + `make precommit`)\n\nBoth are in the inbox (`prompts/`), not `prompts/in-progress/`.\n\n## Decomposition decisions (why 2, not the spec's 4)\n\nThe spec's Suggested Decomposition table proposes 4 prompts (fix main.go / fix run-task / tests / changelog+precommit). I collapsed this to 2:\n\n1. **Implementation + tests in one prompt** — the two entry-point changes are near-identical, coupled by the same defect, and must ship together (the spec's atomic-batch constraint says \"the fix lives in this repo's two entry points only\"). The regression tests belong with their implementation — splitting tests into their own prompt would have been a dependency-heavy no-op. The whole thing is ~20 lines of production change + two small Ginkgo specs.\n2. **CHANGELOG + `make precommit` in a separate final prompt** — the CLAUDE.md convention is to write the `## Unreleased` entry *before* the slow final gate, and the spec's AC 4/5 are distinct deliverables. Keeping the fast `make test` loop in prompt 1 separate from the slow precommit gate in prompt 2 is the natural split.\n\nPer the Sizing Guide, 2 prompts is right for a single feature (2-3 range).\n\n## Key design decisions (surfaced for the reviewer)\n\n- **Test observability was the one real ambiguity.** `main.go`'s `application.Run` builds the deliverer internally (`createDeliverer`): empty `TASK_ID` → Noop (not inspectable), non-empty → real Kafka SyncProducer (needs a broker). So an end-to-end test through `Run` cannot assert on the delivered `AgentResultInfo` without a real Kafka broker or a new injection seam. I resolved this by **extracting the nil-result delivery into an unexported `application.deliverNilResult(ctx, deliverer) error` method in both entry points** (mirroring the agent lib's `unsupportedPhase`), and unit-testing that method directly with the counterfeiter fake `github.com/bborbe/agent/mocks.AgentResultDeliverer` — the same external-mock pattern this repo already uses with `kafkamocks`. This asserts exactly what the ACs demand (`Status == Failed`, phase name in `Message`, no error) without Kafka. No new injection seam, no re-architecting.\n- **Test package changed `main_test` → `main`** in both `main_test.go` files (required to reach the unexported method). This deviates from the go-testing-guide's external-package preference; it's the standard tradeoff for testing unexported entry-point internals, and the requirements state the rationale inline.\n- **Message text kept as-is**: `\"agent run returned nil result (all steps skipped for phase %s)\"` becomes the delivered `Message` — minimal diff, still names the phase, and operators already recognize it.\n- **No `PrintResult` on the nil path** — mirrors `unsupportedPhase` (which doesn't print); the failure is diagnosable in the task body per desired behavior #3. Spec doesn't require printing.\n- **Deliver failure** returns `errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, \"deliver nil-result failure\")` — matches the spec Failure Modes table's `deliver ... failure` log signature (controller retries, bounded).\n- **No scenario prompt** — the scenario-writing four-condition test fails on condition (a): the behavior is fully unit-testable with the fake deliverer, so no `scenarios/NNN-*.md` is warranted. The operator-executable deploy checks stay on the spec's Verification ladder.\n\n## Verification of symbols (all read from real source before writing)\n\n- `agentlib.ResultDeliverer` / `DeliverResult(ctx, AgentResultInfo) error`, `AgentResultInfo{Status, Output, Message, NextPhase, ContinueToNext}`, `AgentStatusFailed = \"failed\"`, `agentlib.Result{Status, NextPhase, Message, ContinueToNext}` — from `github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.84.1`\n- `errors.Wrapf` / `errors.New` signatures — from `github.com/bborbe/errors@v1.5.21`\n- `mocks.AgentResultDeliverer` fake API (`DeliverResultReturns`, `DeliverResultCallCount`, `DeliverResultArgsForCall`) — from the lib's generated mocks\n- Sibling entry-point check: `grep` found a third `application.Run` in `cmd/create-tasks/main.go`, but it never calls `agent.Run` and has no nil-result guard — explicitly marked out-of-scope in prompt 1. `hideGit` is not set (`workflow: direct`), and no git commands appear in any `<verification>` anyway.\n\n## Docs referenced in `<context>` (in-container paths)\n\n- Prompt 1: `coding/docs/go-error-wrapping-guide.md`, `go-testing-guide.md`, `go-doc-best-practices.md`, `definition-of-done.md`; project `docs/dod.md`\n- Prompt 2: `coding/docs/changelog-guide.md`; project `docs/dod.md`\n\n## Pattern inlined because no doc exists\n\nThe \"entry point delivers a `Failed` result via the deliverer on the nil-result path\" pattern (build `Result` → `DeliverResult(AgentResultInfo{Status, Message})` → wrap deliver error → return nil) is inlined verbatim in prompt 1's `<context>`, sourced from the agent lib's own `unsupportedPhase` exemplar. There is no coding-plugin doc covering this specific entry-point pattern; since it's a direct mirror of an in-repo/live-library exemplar, inlining is appropriate — but if this recurs across agents (trade-analysis, pr-reviewer are cited as copy-paste siblings of this main.go), a short `go-agent-entry-point-result-delivery.md` guide would be worth adding later.\n\n## Constraints repeated in both prompts\n\n- Do NOT change `github.com/bborbe/agent` — fix lives in the two entry points only\n- Do not re-architect the phase model; `NextPhase: \"done\"` stays as-is\n- Pushgateway push stays non-fatal (`Warningf`, never fail the Job)\n- Do NOT commit — dark-factory handles git\n- Existing tests must still pass\n- (Prompt 1 additionally pins both Failure Modes rows: non-nil results route through `PrintResult` unchanged; deliver failures return the wrapped error, never swallowed)\n\n## Verification\n\n- Prompt 1: `make test` at repo root + per-package coverage confirming `deliverNilResult` is 100% covered (both success and error paths)\n- Prompt 2: `grep -n \"nil result\" CHANGELOG.md` above `## v0.9.1` + `make precommit` exits 0 (with the fix-then-rerun-failing-target loop per CLAUDE.md)\n\nSuggested next step: run `/audit-prompt prompts/1-spec-001-fix-nil-result.md` and `/audit-prompt prompts/2-spec-001-changelog-precommit.md` to validate before approving."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: aeec503807722fc25 (use SendMessage with to: 'aeec503807722fc25', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 117357\ntool_uses: 47\nduration_ms: 322955</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8524de8b-d7ea-43c2-94e8-affce53f1549","uuid":"865179e5-d1cf-484d-affc-ad0d0220a95e","timestamp":"2026-09-03T19:34:57.679Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Generate dark-factory prompt files from the approved spec at `specs/in-progress/001-sentry-collector-nil-result.md` (repo-root-relative path; the repo root is your working directory — do NOT prefix with /workspace).\n\n## Mode: NON-INTERACTIVE (daemon-triggered)\n\nYou MUST NOT call AskUserQuestion. This is a daemon-triggered run. Resolve any ambiguity from the spec content alone. If the spec is genuinely under-specified, produce the best-effort decomposition and surface the open questions as comments inside the generated prompts (so the human reviewer catches them at audit time).\n\n## Context\n\n- Spec file path: `specs/in-progress/001-sentry-collector-nil-result.md` (relative to repo root = cwd)\n- Output directory: `prompts/` (the inbox — relative to repo root/cwd; NOT `prompts/in-progress/`, dark-factory moves files on approve)\n- You have full re