{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a4cd6d4eef9b2f0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstatus: generating\n3\tapproved: \"2026-09-03T19:27:29Z\"\n4\tgenerating: \"2026-09-03T19:29:15Z\"\n5\tbranch: dark-factory/sentry-collector-nil-result\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## Summary\n9\t\n10\t- `agent.Run` returns `(nil, nil)` when a phase's steps are all skipped (`ShouldRun=false`) or the phase has no registered steps\n11\t- Both entry points convert that nil result into a hard error → Job exits 1 → Job-controller retry loop (observed on nukeprod, task `1363bb29-9af1-5c8d-834f-ca9e1bdd87b3`)\n12\t- The guard's own comment says \"treat as a no-op completion rather than panicking\", but the implementation returns an error — the comment/code contradiction is the defect\n13\t- Fix: deliver a `Failed` result to the task (terminal state) and exit 0 (no controller retry), mirroring the agent lib's `unsupportedPhase` pattern\n14\t- Regression test required in both `main_test.go` and `cmd/run-task/main_test.go`\n15\t\n16\t## Problem\n17\t\n18\t`sentry-collector-agent` Job pods for task `1363bb29-9af1-5c8d-834f-ca9e1bdd87b3` crash-retry looped on nukeprod (`K8sPodStatus` critical alert, 2026-08-27, recurring since 2026-08-26). The loop wastes cluster resources, keeps the alert firing, and the task never reaches a terminal state — so the underlying Sentry issue it was meant to triage never gets resolved.\n19\t\n20\t### Reproduction\n21\t\n22\tMechanism (verified by reading the code, 2026-09-03):\n23\t\n24\t1. `StepRunner.Run` (`github.com/bborbe/agent`, `agent_runner.go:38-85`) walks a phase's steps; when `ShouldRun` returns `false` (e.g. the phase's output section `## Analysis` already exists from a prior run), the step is skipped. When every step is skipped, `lastResult` stays nil and the runner returns `(nil, nil)`.\n25\t2. `Agent.Run` (`agent_agent.go:45-110`) forwards that: `result == nil → return lastResult, nil`.\n26\t3. Both entry points in this repo treat the nil result as a hard failure:\n27\t   - `main.go:305-314` — records `AgentStatusFailed` + duration, then `return errors.Errorf(ctx, \"agent run returned nil result (all steps skipped for phase %s)\", a.Phase)`\n28\t   - `cmd/run-task/main.go:125-133` — same `errors.Errorf` (no metrics)\n29\t4. A returned error makes the process exit 1 → the Job-controller re-creates the Job pod → repeat until the configured backoff limit. Nothing is ever delivered to the task, so it stays `in_progress` and keeps being re-dispatched.\n30\t\n31\tVersion context: the incident (2026-08-26/27) ran on the then-deployed build; the identical guard is present in both `v0.9.0` (7486981) and current `origin/master` `v0.9.1` (f6fa861) — reproduced on both. Live check 2026-09-03: no `sentry` Jobs/pods on nukeprod today (the v0.7.3 `NextPhase: \"done\"` fix cleared the loop), both Config CRDs (`sentry-collector-agent`, `sentry-analyzer-agent`) point at `docker.prod.nuke.benjamin-borbe.de:443/agent-sentry-issue-analyzer:prod`. The 2026-08-27 Job log excerpt showing the exit-1/re-creation is not retrievable in this session; the mechanism is pinned by code evidence below.\n32\t\n33\t**Expected vs Actual**\n34\t\n35\t- Expected (per the guard's own comment at `main.go:307-308`): a stepless phase is a no-op completion — no crash, no retry.\n36\t- Actual: `errors.Errorf` → exit 1 → Job-controller retry loop; task never reaches a terminal state.\n37\t\n38\tThe agent lib itself shows the canonical semantic-failure pattern at `agent_agent.go:135-155` (`unsupportedPhase`): deliver a `Failed` result via the deliverer, return `(result, nil)` — the process exits 0 and the task is closed out. This repo's guards do the opposite.\n39\t\n40\t## Goal\n41\t\n42\tA `sentry-collector` task whose phase has no registered steps (or all steps skipped) exits the Job cleanly, delivers a `Failed` result so the task reaches a terminal state, and never re-enters the controller retry loop.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- [ ] `main.go` nil-result path delivers a `Failed` result via the deliverer whose message names the phase, and returns without error (exit 0) — evidence: `go test` nil-result case asserts `AgentResultInfo.Status == Failed` and `message` contains the phase name\n47\t- [ ] `cmd/run-task/main.go` nil-result path behaves identically (deliver `Failed` naming the phase, exit 0) — evidence: `cmd/run-task` nil-result test asserts the same `Status == Failed` + phase-name-in-message\n48\t- [ ] Regression tests in `main_test.go` and `cmd/run-task/main_test.go` exercise the nil-result path and assert delivered `Status == Failed`, message contains the phase name, and no error returned — evidence: `go test -run <nil-result case> ./...` exits 0 with those assertions\n49\t- [ ] `make precommit` exits 0\n50\t- [ ] Behavior documented in CHANGELOG.md under `## Unreleased` — evidence: `grep -n \"nil result\" CHANGELOG.md` finds the entry above `## v0.9.1`\n51\t\n52\t## Verification\n53\t\n54\t### Container-executable\n55\t\n56\t- `make precommit` exits 0\n57\t- New tests: `go test ./...` passes with the added nil-result cases\n58\t\n59\t### Operator-executable\n60\t\n61\t- Deploy dev (`BRANCH=dev make buca`), run a task whose phase would produce nil result, confirm the Job exits 0 (no retry) and the task shows a failed/terminal state\n62\t- Deploy prod (`BRANCH=prod make buca`), confirm no new Failed `sentry-collector-agent` Job entries and `K8sPodStatus` stays clear\n63\t\n64\t## Desired Behavior\n65\t\n66\t1. A phase with zero registered steps or all steps skipped produces a delivered `Failed` result, not a crash and not a silent no-op\n67\t2. The process exits 0 on this path — no Job-controller retry\n68\t3. The delivered message names the phase so the failure is diagnosable in the task body\n69\t4. Job metrics are recorded (`AgentStatusFailed` + duration) as today in `main.go`; `cmd/run-task` stays consistent with its current metrics-free shape\n70\t5. The pushgateway deferred push (if configured) still fires on this path — it must not be bypassed\n71\t\n72\t## Constraints\n73\t\n74\t- Do not change the agent lib (`github.com/bborbe/agent`) — the fix lives in this repo's two entry points\n75\t- Do not re-architect the phase model; the collector's `NextPhase: \"done\"` behavior (v0.7.3) stays as-is\n76\t- Keep the pushgateway push non-fatal (`Warningf`, never fail the Job on push error)\n77\t\n78\t## Failure Modes\n79\t\n80\t| Trigger | Expected | Recovery |\n81\t|---|---|---|\n82\t| Deliver of the `Failed` result fails (transient network) | Error returned, Job exits non-zero, controller retries (bounded) | `kubectlnukeprod -n prod logs <job pod>` shows the wrapped deliver error (`deliver ... failure`); retry delivers on next attempt |\n83\t| A future lib change returns a different nil shape | Guard still routes non-nil results through `PrintResult` unchanged | Regression test on the nil path fails → caught in review |\n84\t\n85\t## Suggested Decomposition\n86\t\n87\t| # | Prompt focus | Covers DBs | Covers ACs | Depends on |\n88\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n89\t| 1 | Fix `main.go` nil-result branch: deliver `Failed` (phase in message) + exit 0, keep metrics | 1-5 | 1, 4, 5 | — |\n90\t| 2 | Fix `cmd/run-task/main.go` nil-result branch identically | 1-5 | 2, 4, 5 | 1 |\n91\t| 3 | Regression tests for both entry points (Status == Failed, phase in message, exit 0) | 1, 2, 3 | 3, 4 | 1, 2 |\n92\t| 4 | `make precommit` green + CHANGELOG entry under `## Unreleased` | 5 | 4, 5 | 1-3 |\n93\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-96649b4954fa9c1e","session_id":"8524de8b-d7ea-43c2-94e8-affce53f1549","uuid":"3b2370f7-8454-4f10-b0ed-1e48549ba439","timestamp":"2026-09-03T19:35:05.637Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-auditor","task_description":"Audit prompt 1 nil-result fix"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a79c19686fe5594e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tspec: [\"001-sentry-collector-nil-result\"]\n3\tstatus: draft\n4\tcreated: \"2026-09-03T19:30:00Z\"\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t# Deliver a Failed result instead of erroring when a phase has no runnable steps\n8\t\n9\t<summary>\n10\t- A phase whose steps are all skipped (or that has no registered steps) no longer crashes the Job — both entry points now deliver a `Failed` result to the task instead of returning an error\n11\t- The delivered result's message names the phase, so the failure is diagnosable in the task body\n12\t- The process exits 0 on this path, so the Job-controller stops re-creating the pod and the task reaches a terminal state (no retry loop)\n13\t- The Kafka entry point keeps recording `AgentStatusFailed` + duration metrics exactly as it does today\n14\t- The local-CLI entry point behaves identically and stays metrics-free\n15\t- The pushgateway deferred push (if configured) still fires on this path\n16\t- A transient deliver failure is wrapped and returned, so the controller still retries (bounded) instead of the error being swallowed\n17\t- Regression tests in both entry-point test suites assert the delivered status is `Failed`, the message contains the phase name, and no error is returned\n18\t- Non-nil results continue to route through result printing unchanged\n19\t</summary>\n20\t\n21\t<objective>\n22\tMake a phase with no runnable steps a clean, terminal completion: both entry points deliver a `Failed` result naming the phase via the existing deliverer and return without error (exit 0), so the Job stops crash-retrying and the task reaches a terminal state. This mirrors the agent lib's `unsupportedPhase` pattern instead of the current error-return that drives the Job-controller retry loop (spec 001).\n23\t</objective>\n24\t\n25\t<context>\n26\tRead `/home/node/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (YOLO container conventions) before making changes.\n27\t\n28\tRead the coding plugin docs before implementing:\n29\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-error-wrapping-guide.md` — all error wrapping uses `errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, ...)` from `github.com/bborbe/errors`; never `fmt.Errorf` in production code\n30\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md` — Ginkgo v2 + Gomega + Counterfeiter mocks at interface boundaries\n31\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-doc-best-practices.md` — doc comment on the new method\n32\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/definition-of-done.md` — coverage rules (new code >= 80%)\n33\t- `/workspace/docs/dod.md` — project definition of done\n34\t\n35\tRead these project files fully before changing them:\n36\t- `main.go` — the `application.Run` method (the nil-result branch is the `if result == nil {` block inside `Run`), the `createDeliverer` method, and the `application` struct (`Phase domain.TaskPhase` field)\n37\t- `cmd/run-task/main.go` — its `Run` method and identical nil-result branch\n38\t- `main_test.go` and `cmd/run-task/main_test.go` — the existing Ginkgo suite scaffolding you will extend\n39\t\n40\tOut of scope: `cmd/create-tasks/main.go` never calls `agent.Run` (it publishes create-task commands from an alerts file), so it has no nil-result guard and needs no change — the spec's constraint fixes only the two agent-running entry points.\n41\t\n42\tCanonical pattern to mirror — the agent lib's `unsupportedPhase` (source: `$(go env GOMODCACHE)/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.84.1/agent_agent.go`, reproduced verbatim):\n43\t\n44\t```go\n45\t// unsupportedPhase publishes a Failed result with a clear message.\n46\tfunc (a *Agent) unsupportedPhase(\n47\t\tctx context.Context,\n48\t\tphaseName domain.TaskPhase,\n49\t\tdeliverer ResultDeliverer,\n50\t) (*Result, error) {\n51\t\tdisplay := string(phaseName)\n52\t\tif display == \"\" {\n53\t\t\tdisplay = \"(empty)\"\n54\t\t}\n55\t\tresult := &Result{\n56\t\t\tStatus:  AgentStatusFailed,\n57\t\t\tMessage: fmt.Sprintf(\"unsupported entry phase: %s\", display),\n58\t\t}\n59\t\tif err := deliverer.DeliverResult(ctx, AgentResultInfo{\n60\t\t\tStatus:  result.Status,\n61\t\t\tMessage: result.Message,\n62\t\t}); err != nil {\n63\t\t\treturn result, errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, \"deliver unsupported-phase\")\n64\t\t}\n65\t\treturn result, nil\n66\t}\n67\t```\n68\t\n69\tThe delivery contract (source: `agent_result-deliverer.go` and `agent_status.go` in the same module, reproduced verbatim):\n70\t\n71\t```go\n72\t// ResultDeliverer publishes an agent step result back to the task controller.\n73\ttype ResultDeliverer interface {\n74\t\tDeliverResult(ctx context.Context, result AgentResultInfo) error\n75\t}\n76\t\n77\ttype AgentResultInfo struct {\n78\t\tStatus         AgentStatus\n79\t\tOutput         string // body content (typically heading + fenced JSON)\n80\t\tMessage        string // human-readable status; used by failure/needs_input paths\n81\t\tNextPhase      string\n82\t\tContinueToNext bool\n83\t}\n84\t\n85\tconst AgentStatusFailed AgentStatus = \"failed\"\n86\t```\n87\t\n88\tCurrent nil-result branch in `main.go` (inside `Run`, after `agent.Run(...)`):\n89\t\n90\t```go\n91\t\tif result == nil {\n92\t\t\t// agent.Run returns (nil, nil) when every step in the phase skipped\n93\t\t\t// (ShouldRun=false, e.g. the phase's output section already exists from\n94\t\t\t// a prior run) — treat as a no-op completion rather than panicking.\n95\t\t\tjobMetrics.RecordRun(agentlib.AgentStatusFailed)\n96\t\t\tjobMetrics.RecordDuration(time.Since(start))\n97\t\t\treturn errors.Errorf(\n98\t\t\t\tctx,\n99\t\t\t\t\"agent run returned nil result (all steps skipped for phase %s)\",\n100\t\t\t\ta.Phase,\n101\t\t\t)\n102\t\t}\n103\t```\n104\t\n105\tCurrent nil-result branch in `cmd/run-task/main.go` (inside `Run`):\n106\t\n107\t```go\n108\t\tif result == nil {\n109\t\t\t// agent.Run returns (nil, nil) when every step in the phase skipped\n110\t\t\t// (ShouldRun=false, e.g. the phase's output section already exists from\n111\t\t\t// a prior run) — treat as a no-op completion rather than panicking.\n112\t\t\treturn errors.Errorf(\n113\t\t\t\tctx,\n114\t\t\t\t\"agent run returned nil result (all steps skipped for phase %s)\",\n115\t\t\t\ta.Phase,\n116\t\t\t)\n117\t\t}\n118\t```\n119\t</context>\n120\t\n121\t<requirements>\n122\t1. `main.go` — add the `\"fmt\"` standard-library import to the import block (the stdlib group currently contains `\"context\"`, `\"os\"`, `\"time\"`).\n123\t\n124\t2. `main.go` — replace the nil-result branch shown in `<context>` with:\n125\t\n126\t```go\n127\t\tif result == nil {\n128\t\t\t// agent.Run returns (nil, nil) when every step in the phase skipped\n129\t\t\t// (ShouldRun=false, e.g. the phase's output section already exists from\n130\t\t\t// a prior run) or the phase has no registered steps. Deliver a Failed\n131\t\t\t// result so the task reaches a terminal state, then exit 0 — a no-op\n132\t\t\t// completion, never a controller retry (mirrors agent-lib unsupportedPhase).\n133\t\t\tjobMetrics.RecordRun(agentlib.AgentStatusFailed)\n134\t\t\tjobMetrics.RecordDuration(time.Since(start))\n135\t\t\treturn a.deliverNilResult(ctx, deliverer)\n136\t\t}\n137\t```\n138\t\n139\tKeep the two `jobMetrics.RecordRun(...)` / `jobMetrics.RecordDuration(...)` calls exactly where they are — they must still record `AgentStatusFailed` + duration on this path. Do NOT touch the pushgateway `defer pusher.PushContext(ctx)` block at the top of `Run` — it is a `defer` and already fires on every return path, including this one; it must stay non-fatal (`Warningf` on error).\n140\t\n141\t3. `main.go` — add this method to `application` (place it immediately after the `Run` method):\n142\t\n143\t```go\n144\t// deliverNilResult publishes a Failed result for a phase whose steps all\n145\t// skipped or were never registered (agent.Run returned (nil, nil)), naming\n146\t// the phase so the failure is diagnosable in the task body. Returns nil on\n147\t// success so the process exits 0 and the Job never re-enters the controller\n148\t// retry loop; a deliver failure is wrapped and returned so the controller\n149\t// retries (bounded).\n150\tfunc (a *application) deliverNilResult(\n151\t\tctx context.Context,\n152\t\tdeliverer agentlib.ResultDeliverer,\n153\t) error {\n154\t\tfailedResult := &agentlib.Result{\n155\t\t\tStatus:  agentlib.AgentStatusFailed,\n156\t\t\tMessage: fmt.Sprintf(\"agent run returned nil result (all steps skipped for phase %s)\", a.Phase),\n157\t\t}\n158\t\tif err := deliverer.DeliverResult(ctx, agentlib.AgentResultInfo{\n159\t\t\tStatus:  failedResult.Status,\n160\t\t\tMessage: failedResult.Message,\n161\t\t}); err != nil {\n162\t\t\treturn errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, \"deliver nil-result failure\")\n163\t\t}\n164\t\treturn nil\n165\t}\n166\t```\n167\t\n168\tThis uses only existing primitives: `agentlib.AgentStatusFailed`, `agentlib.Result` (fields `Status` + `Message`), `agentlib.AgentResultInfo`, the already-imported `errors` package (`github.com/bborbe/errors`), and the `fmt` package added in step 1. Keep the error-wrap message exactly `\"deliver nil-result failure\"` — the spec's Failure Modes table documents operators grepping Job logs for `deliver ... failure`.\n169\t\n170\t4. `cmd/run-task/main.go` — add the `\"fmt\"` standard-library import to the import block (the stdlib group currently contains `\"context\"`, `\"os\"`).\n171\t\n172\t5. `cmd/run-task/main.go` — replace the nil-result branch shown in `<context>` with:\n173\t\n174\t```go\n175\t\tif result == nil {\n176\t\t\t// agent.Run returns (nil, nil) when every step in the phase skipped\n177\t\t\t// (ShouldRun=false, e.g. the phase's output section already exists from\n178\t\t\t// a prior run) or the phase has no registered steps. Deliver a Failed\n179\t\t\t// result so the task reaches a terminal state, then exit 0 — a no-op\n180\t\t\t// completion, never a controller retry (mirrors agent-lib unsupportedPhase).\n181\t\t\treturn a.deliverNilResult(ctx, deliverer)\n182\t\t}\n183\t```\n184\t\n185\t6. `cmd/run-task/main.go` — add the identical `deliverNilResult` method to `application` (immediately after `Run`), same body as step 3. This entry point has no metrics — the method carries none, exactly as written.\n186\t\n187\t7. `main_test.go` — change the package declaration from `package main_test` to `package main` (required so the test can reach the unexported `application.deliverNilResult`; the existing suite scaffolding — `TestSuite`, the `//go:generate` line, and the `Compiles` spec — stays as-is). Add the imports: `\"context\"`, `agentlib \"github.com/bborbe/agent\"`, `agentmocks \"github.com/bborbe/agent/mocks\"`, `\"github.com/bborbe/errors\"`, `\"github.com/bborbe/vault-cli/pkg/domain\"`. Add this `Describe` block to the suite:\n188\t\n189\t```go\n190\tvar _ = Describe(\"application\", func() {\n191\t\tDescribe(\"deliverNilResult\", func() {\n192\t\t\tvar (\n193\t\t\t\tctx       context.Context\n194\t\t\t\tdeliverer *agentmocks.AgentResultDeliverer\n195\t\t\t)\n196\t\n197\t\t\tBeforeEach(func() {\n198\t\t\t\tctx = context.Background()\n199\t\t\t\tdeliverer = &agentmocks.AgentResultDeliverer{}\n200\t\t\t})\n201\t\n202\t\t\tIt(\"delivers a Failed result naming the phase and returns nil\", func() {\n203\t\t\t\tapp := &application{Phase: domain.TaskPhase(\"planning\")}\n204\t\t\t\terr := app.deliverNilResult(ctx, deliverer)\n205\t\t\t\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n206\t\t\t\tExpect(deliverer.DeliverResultCallCount()).To(Equal(1))\n207\t\t\t\t_, info := deliverer.DeliverResultArgsForCall(0)\n208\t\t\t\tExpect(info.Status).To(Equal(agentlib.AgentStatusFailed))\n209\t\t\t\tExpect(info.Message).To(ContainSubstring(\"planning\"))\n210\t\t\t})\n211\t\n212\t\t\tIt(\"wraps and returns a deliver failure\", func() {\n213\t\t\t\tdeliverer.DeliverResultReturns(errors.New(ctx, \"simulated deliver failure\"))\n214\t\t\t\tapp := &application{Phase: domain.TaskPhase(\"planning\")}\n215\t\t\t\terr := app.deliverNilResult(ctx, deliverer)\n216\t\t\t\tExpect(err).To(HaveOccurred())\n217\t\t\t\tExpect(err.Error()).To(ContainSubstring(\"deliver nil-result failure\"))\n218\t\t\t\tExpect(deliverer.DeliverResultCallCount()).To(Equal(1))\n219\t\t\t})\n220\t\t})\n221\t})\n222\t```\n223\t\n224\t`agentmocks.AgentResultDeliverer` is the counterfeiter fake shipped by `github.com/bborbe/agent/mocks` — the same external-mock pattern this repo already uses with `github.com/bborbe/kafka/mocks`. Do not add any `//counterfeiter:generate` directive; this repo has none and `make precommit`'s `generate` target only regenerates the doc-only root `mocks/mocks.go`.\n225\t\n226\t8. `cmd/run-task/main_test.go` — apply the identical changes as step 7: package `main_test` → `main`, add the same imports, add the same `Describe(\"application\")` / `deliverNilResult` block. The existing `TestSuite` scaffolding stays as-is.\n227\t\n228\t9. Before finishing: run `make test` from the repo root (this repo has a single go.mod; `make test` runs `go test -mod=mod -cover ./...` across all packages, which includes both entry-point suites). It must pass. Then walk each spec acceptance criterion against the change:\n229\t   - `main.go` nil-result path delivers a `Failed` result via the deliverer whose message names the phase, and returns without error (exit 0)\n230\t   - `cmd/run-task/main.go` nil-result path behaves identically\n231\t   - Regression tests in `main_test.go` and `cmd/run-task/main_test.go` assert delivered `Status == Failed`, message contains the phase name, and no error returned\n232\t   - Job metrics (`AgentStatusFailed` + duration) still recorded in `main.go`; pushgateway deferred push not bypassed; `cmd/run-task` stays metrics-free\n233\t</requirements>\n234\t\n235\t<constraints>\n236\t- Do NOT change the agent lib `github.com/bborbe/agent` — the fix lives in this repo's two entry points only\n237\t- Do not re-architect the phase model; the collector's `NextPhase: \"done\"` behavior stays as-is\n238\t- Keep the pushgateway push non-fatal (`Warningf`, never fail the Job on push error)\n239\t- Do NOT commit — dark-factory handles git\n240\t- Existing tests must still pass\n241\t- Non-nil results must continue to route through `jobMetrics.RecordRun(result.Status)` + `agentlib.PrintResult(ctx, result)` unchanged (spec Failure Modes, row 2)\n242\t- A failed deliver must return the wrapped error (Job exits non-zero, controller retries bounded) — never swallow it (spec Failure Modes, row 1)\n243\t- No operator-side steps belong in this prompt — the container agent has no operator\n244\t</constraints>\n245\t\n246\t<verification>\n247\tRun `make test` from the repo root. Must exit 0.\n248\t\n249\tCoverage of the changed code (new method must be fully covered by both the success and the error specs added in steps 7-8):\n250\t```\n251\tgo test -mod=mod -coverprofile=/tmp/cover-main.out . && go tool cover -func=/tmp/cover-main.out\n252\tgo test -mod=mod -coverprofile=/tmp/cover-runtask.out ./cmd/run-task && go tool cover -func=/tmp/cover-runtask.out\n253\t```\n254\tConfirm `deliverNilResult` shows 100% coverage in both packages.\n255\t</verification>\n256\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-96649b4954fa9c1e","session_id":"8524de8b-d7ea-43c2-94e8-affce53f1549","uuid":"6701a76c-7062-4b37-b2a4-deeff66b5277","timestamp":"2026-09-03T19:35:05.641Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-auditor","task_description":"Audit prompt 1 nil-result fix"}
