{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a644a785953d6ae2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tspec: [\"001-sentry-collector-nil-result\"]\n3\tstatus: draft\n4\tcreated: \"2026-09-03T19:30:00Z\"\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t# Deliver a Failed result instead of erroring when a phase has no runnable steps\n8\t\n9\t<summary>\n10\t- A phase whose steps are all skipped (or that has no registered steps) no longer crashes the Job — both entry points now deliver a `Failed` result to the task instead of returning an error\n11\t- The delivered result's message names the phase, so the failure is diagnosable in the task body\n12\t- The process exits 0 on this path, so the Job-controller stops re-creating the pod and the task reaches a terminal state (no retry loop)\n13\t- The Kafka entry point keeps recording `AgentStatusFailed` + duration metrics exactly as it does today\n14\t- The local-CLI entry point behaves identically and stays metrics-free\n15\t- The pushgateway deferred push (if configured) still fires on this path\n16\t- A transient deliver failure is wrapped and returned, so the controller still retries (bounded) instead of the error being swallowed\n17\t- Regression tests in both entry-point test suites assert the delivered status is `Failed`, the message contains the phase name, and no error is returned\n18\t- Non-nil results continue to route through result printing unchanged\n19\t</summary>\n20\t\n21\t<objective>\n22\tMake a phase with no runnable steps a clean, terminal completion: both entry points deliver a `Failed` result naming the phase via the existing deliverer and return without error (exit 0), so the Job stops crash-retrying and the task reaches a terminal state. This mirrors the agent lib's `unsupportedPhase` pattern instead of the current error-return that drives the Job-controller retry loop (spec 001).\n23\t</objective>\n24\t\n25\t<context>\n26\tRead `/home/node/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (YOLO container conventions) before making changes.\n27\t\n28\tRead the coding plugin docs before implementing:\n29\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-error-wrapping-guide.md` — all error wrapping uses `errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, ...)` from `github.com/bborbe/errors`; never `fmt.Errorf` in production code\n30\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md` — Ginkgo v2 + Gomega + Counterfeiter mocks at interface boundaries\n31\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-doc-best-practices.md` — doc comment on the new method\n32\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/definition-of-done.md` — coverage rules (new code >= 80%)\n33\t- `/workspace/docs/dod.md` — project definition of done\n34\t\n35\tRead these project files fully before changing them:\n36\t- `main.go` — the `application.Run` method (the nil-result branch is the `if result == nil {` block inside `Run`), the `createDeliverer` method, and the `application` struct (`Phase domain.TaskPhase` field)\n37\t- `cmd/run-task/main.go` — its `Run` method and identical nil-result branch\n38\t- `main_test.go` and `cmd/run-task/main_test.go` — the existing Ginkgo suite scaffolding you will extend\n39\t\n40\tOut of scope: `cmd/create-tasks/main.go` never calls `agent.Run` (it publishes create-task commands from an alerts file), so it has no nil-result guard and needs no change — the spec's constraint fixes only the two agent-running entry points.\n41\t\n42\tCanonical pattern to mirror — the agent lib's `unsupportedPhase` (source: `$(go env GOMODCACHE)/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.84.1/agent_agent.go`, reproduced verbatim):\n43\t\n44\t```go\n45\t// unsupportedPhase publishes a Failed result with a clear message.\n46\tfunc (a *Agent) unsupportedPhase(\n47\t\tctx context.Context,\n48\t\tphaseName domain.TaskPhase,\n49\t\tdeliverer ResultDeliverer,\n50\t) (*Result, error) {\n51\t\tdisplay := string(phaseName)\n52\t\tif display == \"\" {\n53\t\t\tdisplay = \"(empty)\"\n54\t\t}\n55\t\tresult := &Result{\n56\t\t\tStatus:  AgentStatusFailed,\n57\t\t\tMessage: fmt.Sprintf(\"unsupported entry phase: %s\", display),\n58\t\t}\n59\t\tif err := deliverer.DeliverResult(ctx, AgentResultInfo{\n60\t\t\tStatus:  result.Status,\n61\t\t\tMessage: result.Message,\n62\t\t}); err != nil {\n63\t\t\treturn result, errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, \"deliver unsupported-phase\")\n64\t\t}\n65\t\treturn result, nil\n66\t}\n67\t```\n68\t\n69\tThe delivery contract (source: `agent_result-deliverer.go` and `agent_status.go` in the same module, reproduced verbatim):\n70\t\n71\t```go\n72\t// ResultDeliverer publishes an agent step result back to the task controller.\n73\ttype ResultDeliverer interface {\n74\t\tDeliverResult(ctx context.Context, result AgentResultInfo) error\n75\t}\n76\t\n77\ttype AgentResultInfo struct {\n78\t\tStatus         AgentStatus\n79\t\tOutput         string // body content (typically heading + fenced JSON)\n80\t\tMessage        string // human-readable status; used by failure/needs_input paths\n81\t\tNextPhase      string\n82\t\tContinueToNext bool\n83\t}\n84\t\n85\tconst AgentStatusFailed AgentStatus = \"failed\"\n86\t```\n87\t\n88\tCurrent nil-result branch in `main.go` (inside `Run`, after `agent.Run(...)`):\n89\t\n90\t```go\n91\t\tif result == nil {\n92\t\t\t// agent.Run returns (nil, nil) when every step in the phase skipped\n93\t\t\t// (ShouldRun=false, e.g. the phase's output section already exists from\n94\t\t\t// a prior run) — treat as a no-op completion rather than panicking.\n95\t\t\tjobMetrics.RecordRun(agentlib.AgentStatusFailed)\n96\t\t\tjobMetrics.RecordDuration(time.Since(start))\n97\t\t\treturn errors.Errorf(\n98\t\t\t\tctx,\n99\t\t\t\t\"agent run returned nil result (all steps skipped for phase %s)\",\n100\t\t\t\ta.Phase,\n101\t\t\t)\n102\t\t}\n103\t```\n104\t\n105\tCurrent nil-result branch in `cmd/run-task/main.go` (inside `Run`):\n106\t\n107\t```go\n108\t\tif result == nil {\n109\t\t\t// agent.Run returns (nil, nil) when every step in the phase skipped\n110\t\t\t// (ShouldRun=false, e.g. the phase's output section already exists from\n111\t\t\t// a prior run) — treat as a no-op completion rather than panicking.\n112\t\t\treturn errors.Errorf(\n113\t\t\t\tctx,\n114\t\t\t\t\"agent run returned nil result (all steps skipped for phase %s)\",\n115\t\t\t\ta.Phase,\n116\t\t\t)\n117\t\t}\n118\t```\n119\t</context>\n120\t\n121\t<requirements>\n122\t1. `main.go` — add the `\"fmt\"` standard-library import to the import block (the stdlib group currently contains `\"context\"`, `\"os\"`, `\"time\"`).\n123\t\n124\t2. `main.go` — replace the nil-result branch shown in `<context>` with:\n125\t\n126\t```go\n127\t\tif result == nil {\n128\t\t\t// agent.Run returns (nil, nil) when every step in the phase skipped\n129\t\t\t// (ShouldRun=false, e.g. the phase's output section already exists from\n130\t\t\t// a prior run) or the phase has no registered steps. Deliver a Failed\n131\t\t\t// result so the task reaches a terminal state, then exit 0 — a no-op\n132\t\t\t// completion, never a controller retry (mirrors agent-lib unsupportedPhase).\n133\t\t\tjobMetrics.RecordRun(agentlib.AgentStatusFailed)\n134\t\t\tjobMetrics.RecordDuration(time.Since(start))\n135\t\t\treturn a.deliverNilResult(ctx, deliverer)\n136\t\t}\n137\t```\n138\t\n139\tKeep the two `jobMetrics.RecordRun(...)` / `jobMetrics.RecordDuration(...)` calls exactly where they are — they must still record `AgentStatusFailed` + duration on this path. Do NOT touch the pushgateway `defer pusher.PushContext(ctx)` block at the top of `Run` — it is a `defer` and already fires on every return path, including this one; it must stay non-fatal (`Warningf` on error).\n140\t\n141\t3. `main.go` — add this method to `application` (place it immediately after the `Run` method):\n142\t\n143\t```go\n144\t// deliverNilResult publishes a Failed result for a phase whose steps all\n145\t// skipped or were never registered (agent.Run returned (nil, nil)), naming\n146\t// the phase so 