ing plugin's prompt-generation guidance explicitly recommends inlining load-bearing contracts; verified verbatim against `agent_agent.go:135-155`\n- [x] Coding-plugin docs referenced in `<context>` (go-error-wrapping, go-testing, go-doc-best-practices, definition-of-done) — all exist on disk\n- [x] Project `docs/dod.md` referenced\n- [x] No domain knowledge inlined that should live in project docs\n\n## Code Reference Verification\n| Reference | Status |\n|-----------|--------|\n| `main.go` nil-result branch (context lines 88–103) | Verified verbatim (actual lines 306–317) |\n| `cmd/run-task/main.go` nil-result branch (context lines 105–118) | Verified verbatim (actual lines 125–134) |\n| `main.go` `createDeliverer`, `application.Phase domain.TaskPhase` | Verified (main.go:133, 118) |\n| `cmd/run-task/main.go` `application.Phase domain.TaskPhase`, `deliverer := factory.CreateFileResultDeliverer(...)` | Verified (cmd/run-task/main.go:74, 88; returns `agentlib.ResultDeliverer`, factory.go:91) |\n| `agentlib.unsupportedPhase` (reproduced in context) | Verified verbatim, `agent_agent.go:135-155` |\n| `agentlib.ResultDeliverer` + `DeliverResult(ctx, AgentResultInfo)` | Verified, `agent_result-deliverer.go:15-17` |\n| `agentlib.AgentResultInfo` fields (Status/Output/Message/NextPhase/ContinueToNext) | Verified, `agent_status.go:33+` |\n| `agentlib.AgentStatusFailed AgentStatus = \"failed\"` | Verified, `agent_status.go:24` |\n| `agentlib.Result` fields `Status` + `Message` | Verified, `agent_step.go:45-55` |\n| `agentmocks.AgentResultDeliverer` + `DeliverResultCallCount/ArgsForCall/Returns` | Verified, `mocks/agent-result-deliverer.go` (package `mocks`) |\n| `errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, ...)` / `errors.New(ctx, ...)` (bborbe/errors v1.5.21) | Verified |\n| `domain.TaskPhase` (vault-cli v0.116.2) | Verified, `pkg/domain/task_phase.go:16`, package `domain` |\n| `agentlib.PrintResult(ctx, result)` | Verified, `agent_print-result.go:19` |\n| \"make test runs `go test -mod=mod -cover ./...`\" | Approximately accurate — actual target is `go test -mod=mod -p=1 -cover -race=false $(go list -mod=mod ./... \\| grep -v /vendor/)`; essence (mod=mod, cover, all packages) holds, not load-bearing |\n| \"generate target only regenerates doc-only root `mocks/mocks.go`\" + \"repo has no `//counterfeiter:generate` directives\" | Verified — `Makefile.precommit` generate target recreates `mocks/mocks.go`; only counterfeiter reference is the `//go:generate ... counterfeiter/v6 -generate` runner line (no directives) |\n| \"cmd/create-tasks/main.go never calls `agent.Run`\" | Verified — uses agentlib only for `TaskIdentifier`/`TaskFrontmatter` |\n| Metric-free claim for `cmd/run-task` | Verified — no jobMetrics/prometheus references in cmd/run-task |\n| Version claims (`agent@v0.84.1`) | Verified — matches go.mod require |\n\nNo stale, renamed, or hallucinated references found. Every cited symbol was grepped in the actual module source at the pinned version.\n\n## Coding Guidelines Compliance\n| Guideline | Status |\n|-----------|--------|\n| Error wrapping with `errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, ...)`, no `fmt.Errorf` in production code | Compliant — the new method uses `errors.Wrapf`; `fmt` is used only for `fmt.Sprintf` message construction |\n| Doc comment starts with method name (`deliverNilResult publishes ...`) | Compliant |\n| Ginkgo/Gomega tests, Counterfeiter external mocks at interface boundaries | Compliant — uses `agentmocks.AgentResultDeliverer`, matching the existing `github.com/bborbe/kafka/mocks` precedent in `pkg/factory/factory_test.go:13` |\n| Test-only package-level mutable state | None introduced — N/A |\n| External test package convention (`<pkg>_test`, go-testing-guide.md line ~410) | Deviation — steps 7–8 change `package main_test` → `package main`. Deliberate and necessary (reaching unexported `application.deliverNilResult`), and standard Go practice; flagged as Recommendation R2 |\n\n## YAGNI Pass (scope-creep detector)\n- [x] No opt-out flags, no new config fields, no tunable thresholds, no unrequested branches\n- [x] The message string reuses the exact pre-existing error text (no new vocabulary); the wrap message is pinned by the spec's Failure Modes grep contract\n- [x] Test cases (success + failure) are exactly what the spec's AC evidence demands — nothing extra\n\n## Critical Issues\nNone.\n\n## Recommendations\n1. **Modified `Run` branches are not directly test-covered** (requirements steps 2 and 5, lines 124–137 and 172–183). The new tests cover the extracted `deliverNilResult` helper in isolation (steps 7–8), but the modified `if result == nil { ... return a.deliverNilResult(ctx, deliverer) }` branches inside both `Run` methods — including the preserved `jobMetrics.RecordRun`/`RecordDuration` calls in main.go — are never exercised. This is the standard extract-helper tradeoff; a black-box `Run` test would require faking the whole pipeline (createDeliverer → buildClaudeEnv → validatePreflight → provider.Get → agent.Run) and is not feasible in this repo's shape. Acceptable, but consider adding one line in step 9 noting the branch glue is review-covered (not test-covered), so the gap is a conscious decision rather than an oversight.\n\n2. **`package main_test` → `package main` in both test files** (step 7 line 187, step 8 line 226) deviates from `go-testing-guide.md`'s external-test-package convention. The deviation is justified and correct (the only way to reach the unexported method without re-architecting `Run`), but it is unexplained in the prompt beyond the necessity clause. Suggest instructing the agent to add a one-line comment above the package declaration (e.g. \"internal test package: needed to reach unexported application.deliverNilResult\") so a future author does not \"clean up\" the package back to `main_test` and break the tests.\n\n3. **Minor — `deliverNilResult` is duplicated across the two entry-point binaries** (steps 3 and 6). This matches the repo's existing pattern (both binaries already duplicate preflight, claudeEnv assembly, and struct definitions), so no shared helper is warranted — noted only for completeness, no change needed.\n\n4. **Passing note (spec, not prompt):** the spec's Suggested Decomposition \"Covers ACs\" column is internally inconsistent (row 1 claims ACs 1, 4, 5, but AC4 `make precommit` and AC5 CHANGELOG belong to row 4). The prompt's actual scope is correct (ACs 1–3 in this prompt, ACs 4–5 in the sibling `2-spec-001-changelog-precommit.md`), so no action needed here.\n\n## Strengths\n- Every external symbol is pinned to the real module version and verified verbatim against module source — no hallucinated symbols, no version claims, and the two inlined contracts (`unsupportedPhase`, delivery types) match the actual source byte-for-byte.\n- Sibling entry-point parity is complete: both nil-result sites are changed, and the audit grep confirms there is no third `agent.Run` caller that could silently bypass the fix.\n- Container-autonomy is exemplary: no operator steps, no deploy/rollout work, and the prompt explicitly self-documents the boundary (\"No operator-side steps belong in this prompt — the container agent has no operator\"). The operator verification stays on the spec's ladder.\n- Failure-mode coverage is complete across the prompt set, with the wrap-message string pinned to the spec's log-grep recovery contract.\n- The verification is honest about scope: `make test` + targeted coverage (not a fake `make precommit` gate), with the full gate correctly deferred to the sibling prompt.\n- No scope creep — the change surface is exactly the spec's Goal, nothing more.\n\n## Summary\nAn exemplary prompt: every code reference verified accurate at the pinned module versions, both entry points and all failure modes covered, container-autonomous, and free of scope creep. No critical issues. The only recommendations are the untested branch-glue of the extracted helper (acceptable tradeoff, worth one documenting line) and annotating the justified internal-test-package deviation so it survives future refactors.\n\nRelevant files read during audit: `/workspace/prompts/1-spec-001-fix-nil-result.md`, `/workspace/prompts/2-spec-001-changelog-precommit.md`, `/workspace/specs/in-progress/001-sentry-collector-nil-result.md`, `/workspace/main.go`, `/workspace/main_test.go`, `/workspace/cmd/run-task/main.go`, `/workspace/cmd/run-task/main_test.go`, `/workspace/.dark-factory.yaml`, `/workspace/docs/dod.md`, `/workspace/Makefile.precommit`, plus module sources for `agent@v0.84.1`, `errors@v1.5.21`, and `vault-cli@v0.116.2`."}],"resolvedModel":"deepseek-v4-flash[1m]","totalDurationMs":265949,"totalTokens":79394,"totalToolUseCount":34,"usage":{"input_tokens":51,"cache_creation_input_tokens":512,"cache_read_input_tokens":73728,"output_tokens":5103,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":9,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":25,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
