e in the task body per desired behavior #3.\n- **Deliver failure** returns `errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, \"deliver nil-result failure\")` — matches the spec Failure Modes table's `deliver ... failure` log signature.\n- **No scenario prompt** — the behavior is fully unit-testable with the fake deliverer, so no `scenarios/NNN-*.md` is warranted; operator-executable deploy checks stay on the spec's Verification ladder.\n\n**Symbol verification (all read from real source before writing):** `agentlib.ResultDeliverer`/`DeliverResult`, `AgentResultInfo{Status, Output, Message, NextPhase, ContinueToNext}`, `AgentStatusFailed = \"failed\"`, `agentlib.Result`, `errors.Wrapf`/`errors.New` (bborbe/errors v1.5.21), `mocks.AgentResultDeliverer` fake API, plus a sibling entry-point check — a third `application.Run` in `cmd/create-tasks/main.go` never calls `agent.Run` and has no nil-result guard, explicitly marked out-of-scope in prompt 1.\n\n**Open questions surfaced:** none blocking; the one design ambiguity (test observability) was resolved and documented above. A recurring-pattern note: the \"entry point delivers `Failed` via deliverer on nil-result path\" pattern is inlined verbatim (from the lib's `unsupportedPhase`) because no coding-plugin doc covers it — if it recurs across sibling agents, a `go-agent-entry-point-result-delivery.md` guide would be worth adding.\n\n## Audit Findings\n\n### prompts/1-spec-001-fix-nil-result.md\n\n**Prompt Audit Report: Deliver a Failed result instead of erroring when a phase has no runnable steps**\n**File**: `/workspace/prompts/1-spec-001-fix-nil-result.md`\n**Score**: 9/10 — **Status**: Excellent\n\n**DoD Checklist**\n- [x] `<summary>` present — 9 plain-language bullets, no file paths/struct names/function signatures, each an observable outcome\n- [x] `<objective>` states end state (2 sentences, what + why); the `unsupportedPhase` mention is a reference to an existing lib pattern, not a new design decision\n- [x] `<context>` present with projec